ty communicating ideas\u201d) and **egocentric** perception may impair clear crew dialogue, especially under high workload.\n- C\u2019s **lack of willingness for further education** could affect long\u2011term development and adaptability to evolving aviation technology.\n**What would change my vote:**\n- Concrete evidence that C\u2019s communication issues have led to safety\u2011critical misunderstandings or that his egocentric attitude undermines crew performance.\n- Conversely, strong positive data on D\u2019s teamwork/communication or a mitigation of B\u2019s interpersonal behavior (e.g., proven conflict\u2011resolution training) would make those candidates more competitive.\nGiven the current balance of decisive, calm decision\u2011making, technical understanding, and a clear concern for crew welfare, Candidate\u202fC appears the most suitable overall, pending clarification of the communication concerns.\nMETADATA_JSON:\n{\"agent\": \"agent_2\", \"vote\": \"Candidate C\"}"}
